## ⚠️ Common Pitfalls & Debugging

1. **Infinite Redirect Loops:** Ensure the link's target `url` does not point back to `http://localhost:3000/r/[id]`.
2. **Route Handler Cached Statically:** If you omit `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`, Next.js build will attempt to evaluate `/r/[id]` at build time and freeze it.
3. **`after()` Unhandled Promise:** If your database drops connection, errors thrown inside `after()` do not bubble up to the client (which already received 302). Always wrap asynchronous logic inside `after()` with `try/catch` and log errors.

