### Step 5 · Synchronous Persistence in Message Pipeline

Update `src/server/message-dispatcher.ts` so that when a `CHAT_MESSAGE_SEND` frame arrives, it is saved to PostgreSQL *before* publishing to Redis, guaranteeing persistent monotonic IDs.

```typescript
// In src/server/message-dispatcher.ts:
import { messageRepo } from '../repositories/message-repository.js';

case 'CHAT_MESSAGE_SEND': {
  // 1. Persist to PostgreSQL with client idempotency key
  const saved = await messageRepo.saveMessage(
    message.roomId,
    socket.userId,
    message.content,
    message.clientMsgId
  );

  // 2. Publish to Redis for horizontal fan-out
  await roomManager.publishToRoom({
    originSocketId: socket.id,
    roomId: message.roomId,
    senderId: socket.userId,
    content: message.content,
    clientMsgId: message.clientMsgId,
    serverMsgId: saved.id,
    timestamp: new Date(saved.createdAt).getTime(),
  });

  // 3. Acknowledge back to sender with confirmed DB ID
  socket.send(makeServerEnvelope('ACK', {
    action: 'MESSAGE_PERSISTED',
    clientMsgId: message.clientMsgId,
    serverMsgId: saved.id,
    createdAt: saved.createdAt,
  }));
  break;
}
```

