# Phase 5 — React Client with Axios Interceptors, TanStack Query & Tailwind UI

## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Build a modern React 18 frontend with TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query v5, and Axios. Implement centralized request/response interceptors to automatically attach Bearer tokens, handle automatic logout on HTTP 401, manage optimistic task creation and status toggles, and provide smooth toast notifications.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

### The Axios Interceptor Architecture

Instead of manually attaching `Authorization: Bearer ${token}` to every individual `fetch` call, we configure centralized Axios request and response interceptors:

```
React Component (useMutation) 
       |
       v
[ Axios Request Interceptor ] ---------> Reads JWT from AuthContext/localStorage
       |                                 Appends 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'
       v
[ HTTP Transmission to Spring Boot ]
       |
       v
[ Axios Response Interceptor ] --------> On 200/201: Return response.data
                                       > On 401: Clear token, dispatch LOGOUT,
                                         redirect user to /login
```

### Server-State Management with TanStack Query v5

We avoid storing remote API data in ad-hoc `useState` hooks. TanStack Query v5 manages caching, background re-validation on window focus, and optimistic UI mutations. When a user clicks "Complete Task", the UI updates **instantaneously** (0ms perceived latency). If the network request fails, TanStack Query automatically rolls back the cache to the previous snapshot.

