## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Deliver an end-to-end banking ledger system. Build a modern React 18 frontend with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Lucide icons featuring client-side idempotency key generation, minor unit monetary formatting, and real-time account statements. Implement property-based concurrency tests in JUnit 5 verifying that total system funds are 100% conserved across 500 randomized parallel transfers. Package the architecture into a production-grade multi-stage Docker container and orchestrate the entire distributed stack (PostgreSQL 16, Apache Kafka in KRaft mode, Spring Boot 3.3, and React) via Docker Compose.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

### 1. Property-Based Testing in Financial Engineering
Traditional unit tests assert known test cases (e.g. *"Alice sends $10 to Bob"*). However, distributed systems fail on chaotic permutations: rapid overlapping transfers, concurrent overdrafts, and interleaving thread scheduling.  
**Property-Based Testing** validates universal mathematical invariants:
$$\sum_{a \in \text{All Accounts}} \text{balance}(a)_{\text{start}} \equiv \sum_{a \in \text{All Accounts}} \text{balance}(a)_{\text{end}}$$

Regardless of how many hundreds of transfers succeed or fail due to insufficient funds, **not a single cent can be created or destroyed**.

```
Property Testing Harness:
[ Initial State: 10 Accounts, Total Balance = $100,000.00 ]
                             |
                             v
[ 500 Randomized Parallel Transfers across 16 Threads ]
  (Random source, random destination, random amounts from 1 to 5,000 cents)
                             |
                             v
[ Final State Check: Sum of all account balances MUST EQUAL $100,000.00 ]
```

### 2. Apache Kafka in KRaft Mode (No ZooKeeper)
Traditional Kafka deployments require maintaining an external Apache ZooKeeper quorum, adding substantial operational overhead and startup latency.  
**KRaft (Kafka Raft Metadata)** mode runs the consensus controller directly inside the Kafka broker process using an internal Raft metadata topic (`@metadata`), slashing startup time from 45 seconds to under 4 seconds while simplifying containerized deployments.

### 3. Financial UI Typography & Idempotency Hygiene
- **Client-Side Idempotency Keys:** The frontend generates a UUIDv4 when the transfer modal opens. If a network timeout occurs and the user clicks "Retry", the identical UUIDv4 is sent, preventing accidental double-charges.
- **Monospace Financial Figures:** Tabular financial records must use tabular lining fonts (`font-mono`) so decimal points and currency figures align vertically for visual scannability.

