## 🛠 Step-by-Step Implementation

### Step 1 · Define Command Enums, Operation Types & Domain Structs
Create `internal/state/command.go` defining supported key-value transactions:

```go
package state

import "fmt"

// OpType defines the operation kind on the key-value store.
type OpType string

const (
	OpGet OpType = "GET"
	OpSet OpType = "SET"
	OpDel OpType = "DEL"
)

// Command encapsulates a client transaction submitted to the Raft consensus log.
type Command struct {
	Op       OpType `json:"op"`
	Key      string `json:"key"`
	Value    string `json:"value,omitempty"`
	ClientID string `json:"client_id"`
	Seq      uint64 `json:"seq"`
}

func (c Command) String() string {
	return fmt.Sprintf("Command{Op: %s, Key: %s, Client: %s, Seq: %d}", c.Op, c.Key, c.ClientID, c.Seq)
}

// CommandResult encapsulates the outcome of executing a command on the state machine.
type CommandResult struct {
	Value   string
	Success bool
	Error   string
}
