# Phase 5 — Concurrent Architecture, Crossbeam Ring Buffers & Live Ratatui Terminal Dashboard

## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Build a multi-threaded, real-time terminal user interface (TUI) for your packet sniffer using `ratatui` and `crossterm`. High-throughput network packet sniffing and terminal rendering have fundamentally conflicting execution characteristics: packet capture must run with sub-millisecond latency to avoid kernel buffer saturation, whereas rendering an interactive terminal dashboard requires formatting tables, calculating layout constraints, and synchronizing with the terminal display at 10–30 frames per second (taking 10 to 30 milliseconds per frame).

If packet capture and terminal rendering share a single thread, the sniffer will freeze during every frame draw, dropping tens of thousands of packets! You will decouple ingestion and rendering into a **Multi-Threaded Producer-Consumer Pipeline**: a dedicated high-priority capture thread streams packets from `libpcap` and decodes headers, while an asynchronous UI thread drains events across a bounded channel with a **Drop-on-Full (Load Shedding)** backpressure strategy. You will construct a sleek dashboard with live throughput counters, sortable top-talkers tables (by byte volume, packet count, or session duration), protocol distribution statistics, handle terminal raw mode setup and teardown cleanly with panic hooks, and author automated tests validating UI state and channel decoupling.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

### 1. Decoupled Producer-Consumer Concurrency Architecture
To guarantee zero packet drops during rendering, the capture thread and UI event loop must run on separate OS threads connected by a lock-free, bounded channel:

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        DECOUPLED TELEMETRY PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE                        |
|                                                                                         |
|  +----------------------------------------------------+                                 |
|  | Thread 1: Ingestion & Decoding (Capture Worker)   |                                 |
|  | - libpcap loop (100ms timeout)                     |                                 |
|  | - Zero-copy decode (Ethernet -> IPv4 -> TCP/UDP)   |                                 |
|  | - Creates lightweight PacketSummary (48 bytes)     |                                 |
|  +----------------------------------------------------+                                 |
|                            |                                                            |
|                            | tx.try_send(summary) (Drop on Full / Never Blocks!)        |
|                            v                                                            |
|  +----------------------------------------------------+                                 |
|  | Bounded Synchronization Channel (Capacity = 4096)  |                                 |
|  +----------------------------------------------------+                                 |
|                            |                                                            |
|                            | rx.try_recv() batch drain (up to 512 per tick)             |
|                            v                                                            |
|  +----------------------------------------------------+                                 |
|  | Thread 2: Aggregator & Ratatui Dashboard (UI Loop) |                                 |
|  | - Updates FlowTable with bidirectional metrics     |                                 |
|  | - Computes Top Talkers (sorted by bytes / packets) |                                 |
|  | - Redraws terminal screen at 10 FPS (100ms tick)   |                                 |
|  | - Captures user key events (q, s, p, c)            |                                 |
|  +----------------------------------------------------+                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

**Load-Shedding Backpressure Formula**:
$$\text{Action on Channel Full} = \begin{cases} \text{tx.send(msg)} & \implies \text{Blocks capture thread } \implies \mathbf{FATAL\ PACKET\ DROPS!} \\ \text{tx.try\_send(msg)} & \implies \text{Drops UI sample, capture continues uninterrupted!} \end{cases}$$

### 2. Ratatui Terminal Layout Architecture
The terminal screen area is partitioned into three responsive layout regions using `Layout::default().constraints(...)`:
1. **Header Panel (Height 3)**: Interface name, active BPF filter, total packets captured, total bytes, active flow count, and dropped packet count.
2. **Main Table Area (Min Height 10)**: Top talkers table with columns for Endpoints, Protocol, State, Forward/Reverse Packets, Total Volume, and Duration.
3. **Footer Status Bar (Height 1)**: Interactive keyboard commands (`[q] Quit`, `[b] Sort by Bytes`, `[p] Sort by Packets`, `[c] Clear Table`).

### 3. Terminal Raw Mode & Panic Recovery Safety
Entering raw mode disables terminal canonical line buffering and echo. If the program terminates abruptly (e.g. panics), the terminal remains in raw mode, making the user's shell unresponsive. We install a custom panic hook that restores standard terminal mode before printing panic messages.

