# Phase 4 — Scatter-Gather Query Engine, Parallel Map-Reduce & Aggregation Merging

## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Design, implement, and optimize a distributed **Scatter-Gather Parallel Query Engine** (Distributed Map-Reduce) capable of querying and aggregating records that span all physical shards in your cluster. While direct routing satisfies $>95\%$ of transactional multi-tenant operations, enterprise analytical dashboards, global administrative searches, and platform-wide metrics aggregation inevitably require querying data across **every database node simultaneously**.

Executing cross-shard queries sequentially would compound network latency linearly ($T_{\text{total}} = \sum_{i=1}^N T_i$). Instead, you will build a parallel scatter-gather engine that executes in parallel bounded by the slowest shard ($T_{\text{total}} = \max_{i=1}^N T_i$). You will implement **Pushdown Optimization**: delegating group-by, counting, and partial sorting directly to PostgreSQL engines on each shard so that network traffic is reduced by orders of magnitude. In the Go router layer, you will implement an algebraic aggregator for mathematical reductions (e.g. calculating global averages from partial sums and counts), construct a **$K$-Way Merge Sort** engine using a binary Min-Heap for globally ordered pagination (`ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT K`), and implement configurable partial-failure degradation modes so that a single slow or dead shard cannot freeze global dashboards.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

### 1. Scatter-Gather Parallel Fan-Out Architecture
Visualize how queries fan out to all shards in parallel and merge in router memory:

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                     SCATTER-GATHER (MAP-REDUCE) QUERY PIPELINE                          |
|                                                                                         |
|  Incoming Query: Router.CountEventsByKind(ctx)                                          |
|                               |                                                         |
|             [Fan-out across all shards via errgroup]                                    |
|            /                  |                  \                                      |
|           v                   v                   v                                     |
|     +-----------+       +-----------+       +-----------+                               |
|     |  Shard 0  |       |  Shard 1  |       |  Shard 2  |                               |
|     +-----------+       +-----------+       +-----------+                               |
|     | SELECT    |       | SELECT    |       | SELECT    |                               |
|     | kind, cnt |       | kind, cnt |       | kind, cnt |   <- Pushdown aggregation!    |
|     | GROUP BY  |       | GROUP BY  |       | GROUP BY  |                               |
|     +-----------+       +-----------+       +-----------+                               |
|           \                   |                   /                                     |
|      {'click': 50}      {'click': 30}       {'click': 40}                               |
|      {'view': 100}      {'view': 250}       {'view': 150}                               |
|            \                  |                  /                                      |
|             v                 v                 v                                       |
|             +-----------------------------------+                                       |
|             |   Router Aggregator / Heap Merger |                                       |
|             |   - Sums 'click': 50+30+40 = 120  |                                       |
|             |   - Sums 'view': 100+250+150= 500 |                                       |
|             +-----------------------------------+                                       |
|                               |                                                         |
|                               v                                                         |
|                  Clean Merged Result to Client                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### 2. Algebraic Aggregation Reduction Math
Never average shard averages together! The mathematical mean across $N$ shards requires decomposing into an algebraic pair:
$$\text{COUNT}_{\text{global}} = \sum_{i=1}^N \text{COUNT}_i$$
$$\text{SUM}_{\text{global}} = \sum_{i=1}^N \text{SUM}_i$$
$$\text{AVG}_{\text{global}} = \frac{\sum_{i=1}^N \text{SUM}_i}{\sum_{i=1}^N \text{COUNT}_i}$$
If Shard 0 has 10 records with average 100, and Shard 1 has 1,000 records with average 10, naive averaging yields $(100 + 10)/2 = 55$ (a $450\%$ calculation error!), whereas algebraic reduction correctly computes $(1000 + 10000)/1010 \approx 10.89$.

### 3. $K$-Way Merge Sort Complexity with Min-Heap
When paginating globally across $N$ shards (`LIMIT K`), each shard pushes down its local `LIMIT K`. The Go router merges the $N$ pre-sorted streams using a Min-Heap priority queue:
$$\text{Time Complexity} = \mathcal{O}(K \log N)$$
$$\text{Space Complexity} = \mathcal{O}(N)$$
This eliminates buffering massive datasets into router memory, keeping garbage collection pauses below 10 microseconds.

